e><lpage>378</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s11606-007-0488-6</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Leu MG, Cheung M, Webster TR, et al. Centers speak up: the clinical context for health information technology in the ambulatory care setting. J Gen Intern Med 2008;23:372-8. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18373132</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bodenheimer</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Grumbach</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Electronic technology: a spark to revitalize primary care</article-title><source>Jama</source><year>2003</year><volume>290</volume><fpage>259</fpage><lpage>264</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.290.2.259</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bodenheimer T, Grumbach K. Electronic technology: a spark to revitalize primary care? Jama 2003;290:259-64. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12851283</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Felt-Lisk</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>McHugh</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Howell</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Monitoring local safety-net providers: do they have adequate capacity</article-title><source>Health Aff (Millwood)</source><year>2002</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>283</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1377/hlthaff.21.5.277</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Felt-Lisk S, McHugh M, Howell E. Monitoring local safety-net providers: do they have adequate capacity? Health Aff (Millwood) 2002;21:277-83. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12224892</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gusmano</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Fairbrother</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exploring the limits of the safety net: community health centers and care for the uninsured</article-title><source>Health Aff (Millwood)</source><year>2002</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>188</fpage><lpage>194</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1377/hlthaff.21.6.188</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Gusmano MK, Fairbrother G, Park H. Exploring the limits of the safety net: community health centers and care for the uninsured. Health Aff (Millwood) 2002;21:188-94. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12442854</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="other"><bold>Felland LE, Felt-Lisk S, McHugh M.</bold> Health care access for low-income people: significant safety net gaps remain. Issue Brief Cent Stud Health Syst Change 2004:1-4.</citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knudtson</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Beanlands</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Brophy</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Higginson</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Munt</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Rottger</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Treating the right patient at the right time: access to specialist consultation and non-invasive testing</article-title><source>Can J Cardiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>819</fpage><lpage>824</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Knudtson ML, Beanlands R, Brophy JM, Higginson L, Munt B, Rottger J. Treating the right patient at the right time: access to specialist consultation and non-invasive testing. Can J Cardiol 2006;22:819-24. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16957798</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Consequences of late referral on patient outcomes</article-title><source>Nephrol Dial Transplant</source><year>2000</year><volume>15</volume><issue>Suppl 3</issue><fpage>8</fpage><lpage>13</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Levin A. Consequences of late referral on patient outcomes. Nephrol Dial Transplant 2000;15(Suppl 3):8-13. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11032351</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shaw</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Berker</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Strengths and weaknesses of electronic referral: comparison of data content and clinical value of electronic and paper referrals in dermatology</article-title><source>Br J Gen Pract</source><year>2007</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>223</fpage><lpage>224</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Shaw LJ, de Berker DA. Strengths and weaknesses of electronic referral: comparison of data content and clinical value of electronic and paper referrals in dermatology. Br J Gen Pract 2007;57:223-4. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17359610</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hunt</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Haynes</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanna</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of computer-based clinical decision support systems on physician performance and patient outcomes: a systematic review</article-title><source>Jama</source><year>1998</year><volume>280</volume><fpage>1339</fpage><lpage>1346</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.280.15.1339</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hunt DL, Haynes RB, Hanna SE, Smith K. Effects of computer-based clinical decision support systems on physician performance and patient outcomes: a systematic review. Jama 1998;280:1339-46. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9794315</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Medow</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilt</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dysken</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hillson</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Woods</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Borowsky</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of written and computerized decision support aids for the U.S. agency for health care policy and research depression guidelines on the evaluation of hypothetical clinical scenarios</article-title><source>Med Decis Making</source><year>2001</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>344</fpage><lpage>356</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Medow MA, Wilt TJ, Dysken S, Hillson SD, Woods S, Borowsky SJ. Effect of written and computerized decision support aids for the U.S. agency for health care policy and research depression guidelines on the evaluation of hypothetical clinical scenarios. Med Decis Making 2001;21:344-56. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11575484</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-